Explanation: 
Sort the array so the numbers come in increasing order.
A good array of size n must contain numbers from 1 to n-1.
Check whether every element from index 0 to n-2 is equal to i+1.
Finally, verify that the last two elements are equal, meaning the largest number appears twice

Code:
class Solution {
    public boolean isGood(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        int n=nums.length;
        if(n<2){
            return false;
        }
        for(int i=0;i<n-1;i++){
            if(nums[i]!=i+1){
                return false;
            }
        }
        return nums[n-1]==nums[n-2];
    }
}
